# Context

## Background
Initial commit of the GitPickle workspace. GitPickle is a self-hosted
application for independent Git repository recovery, proposed in
gitpickle.md. Recovery of version 1 archives works without the
original server or GitHub, using native Git and Python 3.

## Why This Way
The Rust workspace is split by layer (domain, application,
adapters, interfaces, CLI) following docs/adr/0001. TLA+
specifications and recorded evidence in spec/ cover archive
commits, job replay, and plan approval. Python tools under
tools/ drive workflows that the Rust executable does not
cover yet; hosting remains under development.
